data absence_carried_by_a_second_representation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "absence_carried_by_a_second_representation" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**absence carried by a second representation of presence** (invalid state: one fact, 'a value is present or not', has more than one authority -- a `none`/`null` sentinel typed by its own rule, an Absent/Missing/Unset carrier whose whole contract is zero-or-one value, an implicit Present wrap or payload extraction inserted differently by the checker and by realization, an Option type or constructor selected by leaf spelling instead of resolved declaration identity, or a cardinality flag restating structure the type already carries. Harm: DESIGN section 3's nicknaming fork at the meaning layer. Consumers disagree about the same value, nested layers (Present(Absent) against Absent) collapse silently, and each fork is later consolidated at a cost its author deferred).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the reason this is classified by contract rather than by spelling: a reason-bearing MissingPermission, a progress or policy state, and a faithful foreign JSON null are NOT this class; a carrier with exactly a zero-or-one-value contract and no independent cause, progress, policy or upstream meaning IS, whatever it is called. The tell is the contract, never a variant-name suffix.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: IF A TYPE'S ONLY INFORMATION IS 'ONE VALUE OR NONE', IT IS std.optional.Optional OR IT NAMES THE INDEPENDENT DISTINCTION THAT JUSTIFIES ITS EXISTENCE.",

    "Rung found at: mitigatable (mitigated by review under the Cardinality / absence conformance domain, `gunbc.design_argument` `conformance_domains`). Ceiling: structurally guaranteed for DAG absence once the sentinel typing and mint routes are deleted by complete consumer cohorts; the foreign-null and reason-bearing meanings remain declared boundaries. Next trigger, at capability grain: a resolved declaration identity for the Optional constructor and type sugar carried through typing, evaluation and every retained realization (roadmap nodes `cardinality-optional-declaration`, `cardinality-native-closure-cutover`, `cardinality-realization-conformance`), with `cardinality-absence-retirement` deleting the rival routes.",

    "RECEIPT 2026-10-13, REMAINING RIVAL ROOTS BY IDENTITY (cardinality-absence-retirement first slice; deletion is the census, no empty cohort). (1) DAG none→LitNull: extdeps.languages.dag.syntax dag_keyword_literals; consumers named on gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.none_literal_is_a_second_spelling_of_absent; blocked on neat-bear-75. (2) Seed one-bit optional-Unit join: v1.std.core with_optional_cardinality and v1.compiler.infer_* uses; replacement is nested Optional inhabitance, not this lane's Occupancy cut. (3) Remaining spelling-keyed HostOption sites, both required deletions: v1.compiler.emit_rust host_option_arm_reading / HostOptionArmSpelledWithoutIdentity (declaration_owns_host_option and is_host_optional_carrier_type are already identity-keyed), and v1.compiler.emit_rust render_rust_diagnostics_carrier_applied, which emits Option keyed on the leaf name NonEmptyDiagnostics rather than a DeclarationRef. Roster gunbc.rust_source_type_bindings rust_host_option_carrier_declarations (v2.std.diagnostic Diagnostics) plus kernel mint identity. Dissolve trigger for the diagnostics site: after host Option emission keys on DeclarationRef (non_empty_diagnostics_dissolve_trigger). Kind-aware binding is keen-raven-120 #13832, not a Cardinality deletion. (4) Kernel Optional mint: gunbc.structural_realization_bindings kernel_optional_mint_name and kernel_mint_declaration_rows (binds std.optional::Optional); v1.compiler.infer kernel_optional_type_node, kernel_optional_owner_declaring, kernel_optional_shape_refusal; witness v2.test.claim.self_host.kernel_optional_mint_binding; neat-bear-75 may delete first. (5) std.constructors::Cardinality = Required | Optional, consumers v2.std.node_query DeclaredField.cardinality and v2.test.claim.parse.variant_field_lowering; seed fork v1.std.core Required | CardOptional is a different enum; delete only after cardinality-carrier-consolidation. (6) Duplicate 0..1 / nonempty: std.algebra ListHeadResult and ListTailResult (not v2.std.algebra, deleted #13860); Diagnostics = None | Some. v2.std.diagnostic NonEmptyDiagnostics is FROZEN (#13900): no independent semantic distinction; it is retained only because render_rust_diagnostics_carrier_applied keys the host Option inner on that type NAME. Required deletions by identity: v2.std.diagnostic::NonEmptyDiagnostics and v1.compiler.emit_rust::render_rust_diagnostics_carrier_applied, after host Option emission keys on DeclarationRef (non_empty_diagnostics_dissolve_trigger). Occupancy is neat-bear-75 after N7 (#13803, #13827 OPEN). (7) v2.std.node::NamedEdgeTargetLookup = Found { target: Node } | Ambiguous | NotFound. Classified under the absence-name rule (analysis §5): NOT a duplicate 0..1 carrier. Ambiguous is an independent search-collision distinction (fold_assembly decode_node_list_conj refuses it as fold_form_list_edge_ambiguous), so the coproduct is not Optional. RECEIPT 2026-10-14 (#13908 standing done for this deletion): the miss arm spelling Absent is retired; the replacement is NotFound. The three-way coproduct and Ambiguous stay. #13905 is discharged: v2.test.claim.fold_encoding fe_lookup_target now matches Found / Ambiguous / NotFound while std.optional Absent is also in scope, and that module emits. Consumers updated with the rename: named_edge_target_lookup, core_edge_target_lookup, edge_target_lookup_step, v2.std.fold_assembly, v2.std.node arrow_signature_order_read and arrow_body_target lookup, v2.std.node_query find_arrow_body_child, v2.std.cardinality loop_bound_measure_target, v2.std.arrow_contract, v2.compiler.use_site_verdict, v2.compiler.service_realization, v2.compiler.infer, v2.compiler.fold_lowering fold_step_body_node, v2.lens.cost.copied_port_derivation, v2.test.claim.fold_encoding fe_lookup_target, v2.test.claim.fold_lowering, v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering. Wildcard-only lookup sites were left. No cardinality-absence migration-allowance roster exists as a named population; do not mint one to delete.",

    "RUNG BY PATH for the realization half (roadmap node `cardinality-realization-conformance`), as enrolled in `v2.test.claim.cardinality_realization_coverage`. Only the evaluator facts are executed by claims there; the seed Rust and native facts are enrolled expectations transcribed from local runs, not re-derived by any instrument yet: the evaluator realizes all ten specimens under an ungated claim (the required workflow does not run it); the seed Rust emit realizes specimens 1-5, 6 (FreeMonoid spelling), 7, and specimens 8 and 9 since gunbc#13898 added the json_unescape_checked rt_function_registry row (before it a run PANICKED rather than refusing at emit time; class registered_realization_missing_its_registry_row_panics_at_runtime), but not the List spelling of specimen 6 (a List under an Optional is erased); the native v2 CLI refuses the entry's whole closure before any shape is reached (located, typed, closure-wide). The seed Rust and native observations are LOCAL runs, not gated, so the rung is the minimum across paths: mitigatable. Trigger, at capability grain: a wet instrument row that runs the seed Rust emit and the native CLI over the specimens and compares each outcome with the coverage rows; the Rust defects are owned by the emitter and inference lanes named in those rows.",


    "RECEIPT 2026-10-15 (cardinality-absence slice 3), ROOT (4) DELETED BY IDENTITY: gunbc.structural_realization_bindings kernel_optional_mint_name and kernel_mint_declaration_rows (replaced by the single row optional_declaration_ref); std.literal_elaboration KernelMintDeclaration, kernel_mint_declaration_for, KernelMintOwnership, kernel_mint_ownership, KernelNamedImportStanding, kernel_named_import_standing; v1.compiler.infer kernel_optional_type_node (and its kernel_bindings insertions), kernel_optional_owner_declaring (now optional_owner_declaring), kernel_optional_shape_refusal (now optional_declaration_shape_refusal), kernel_mint_shape_diagnostics (now optional_declaration_shape_diagnostics); v1.compiler.resolve kernel_named_import_diags, kernel_collision_diags; v1.compiler.emit_info type_decl_kernel_mint_declarer; v1.compiler.emit_rust HostOptionArmBindingAmbiguous. Witnesses: kernel_optional_mint_binding became v2.test.claim.self_host.optional_declaration_binding; kernel_optional_mint_shape_witness became test.claim.optional_declaration_shape_witness (RED and positive controls kept enrolled); infer_kernel_import_collision_witness stays enrolled and now proves the dissolved class (the imported Optional and `T?` do not cross). Remaining roots (1)-(3),(5)-(7) unchanged.",
  ],

